				"approved": false,
				"feedback": [
					"Define a safe recovery policy for older durable generations before adding automatic fallback. /manifest/packages/0 restores an earlier snapshot when current state or referenced content is invalid, but only requires existing revision and provider checks. Those checks cannot recover a later stop decision or prove that arbitrary agent/script work has not already executed. Evidence: pinned revision 2294d5abd0d80fbd4aea2f6b1ba2046ad87ecab1, packages/edge-worker/src/factory/WorkflowRuntime.ts, constructor/resume at character offsets 16000–32000 and stop at 106000–122000: execution position and stopped status belong to the restored run state. This introduces a possible rollback of lifecycle decisions and completed work; no incident is established. Mark fallback recovery explicitly and prevent automatic execution until affected work is reconciled, requesting operator assistance where safe continuation cannot be established. Add restart tests covering a checkpoint followed by completed side effects or an explicit stop, then corruption of the ordinary snapshot. Retaining authorization evidence alone should not authorize replay."
				]
			}
